### Is the 33.1 percent GDP figure cited by Donald Trump on October 30, 2020, calculated as an annualized rate or as a simple quarter-over-quarter percentage change?
Answer: The 33.1 percent GDP figure cited by Donald Trump is calculated as an annualized rate rather than a simple quarter-over-quarter percentage change. According to the provided source, "The U.S. economy grew at a record annualized rate of 33.1% between July and September," whereas on a "non-annual basis," the third-quarter growth was actually 7.4%.

Source URL: https://www.cbsnews.com/news/gdp-q3-growth-33-1-percent/

