Answer: According to the provided search result, the highest quarterly GDP growth rate in United States history since the government began tracking the data in 1947 is 33.1% on an annualized basis. This record was set in the third quarter of 2020, when gross domestic product "grew at an annualized and seasonally adjusted rate of 33.1% between July and September."

Source URL: https://www.cnn.com/2020/10/29/economy/gdp-report-third-quarter/index.html

### What is the highest quarterly GDP growth rate in United States history when measured on a non-annualized, quarter-over-quarter basis?
Answer: According to the provided text, the highest quarterly GDP growth rate in United States history since record-keeping began in 1947 is **7.4%** on a non-annualized, quarter-over-quarter basis. This record was set in the third quarter of 2020; as the article notes, "looking at the quarterly data alone, GDP grew 7.4% from the second to the third quarter," which corresponds to the record-breaking annualized growth rate of 33.1%.

Source URL: https://www.cnn.com/2020/10/29/economy/gdp-report-third-quarter/index.html

