Source URL: https://usafacts.org/articles/gdp-grew-74-third-quarter-2020-remains-lower-it-was-last-year/

### Is the third-quarter 2020 United States GDP growth rate of 33.1 percent "almost triple" the previous record for United States GDP growth?
Answer: No, the third-quarter 2020 GDP growth rate is not "almost triple" the previous record. According to the search result, the actual GDP growth for the third quarter of 2020 was 7.4% (which annualizes to the 33.1% figure), while the highest previous quarterly GDP growth was 3.9% in the first quarter of 1950. This previous record of 3.9% is "almost half of this historic high" of 7.4%, meaning the 2020 growth rate was roughly double—not triple—the previous quarterly record. Additionally, the record for annual GDP growth was 18.9% in 1942, which is also well over half of the 33.1% annualized figure.

Source URL: https://usafacts.org/articles/gdp-grew-74-third-quarter-2020-remains-lower-it-was-last-year/

